From 79ee9fb8dac59bad8fc7855508136cfaf9453aa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:56:36 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/32] Grow: clear read-auto of a member array before changing
 raid_disks

md changes raid_disks of a writable array only (update_raid_disks()
returns -EROFS otherwise).  For a native array freeze() leaves read-auto
behind; for a member of a container it freezes the container and leaves
the member array as it was, often read-auto after assembly.  Changing
raid_disks of a RAID1 member array without a restripe (raid1 just takes
another slot) then fails: "failed to set raid disks".

In reshape_array(), clear read-auto of a member array of external
metadata before setting raid_disks, as a first write would.  A readonly
set by the user stays, and the change is refused as before.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 Grow.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Grow.c b/Grow.c
index 51579021..14c415ee 100644
--- a/Grow.c
+++ b/Grow.c
@@ -3358,6 +3358,16 @@ static int reshape_array(char *container, int fd, char *devname,
 		    array.raid_disks !=
 		    (info->array.raid_disks + info->delta_disks)) {
 			array.raid_disks += info->delta_disks;
+			/*
+			 * md changes raid_disks of a writable array only;
+			 * freeze() clears read-auto of a native array, not
+			 * of a member of a container.
+			 */
+			if (st->ss->external &&
+			    sysfs_get_str(info, NULL, "array_state",
+					  buf, sizeof(buf)) > 0 &&
+			    strncmp(buf, "read-auto", 9) == 0)
+				ioctl(fd, RESTART_ARRAY_RW, 0);
 			if (md_set_array_info(fd, &array) != 0) {
 				pr_err("failed to set raid disks\n");
 				goto release;
